  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1249 PM CDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nSystem today and tomorrow will be exiting the area, but models\ncontinue to show a weaker shortwave moving quickly into the area\nFriday night into early Saturday. This will keep some showers\npossible across the area for a little longer, with the activity\nending from west to east during the day on Saturday. Showers likely\nto be pretty light. Dry for Saturday Night into Monday as a weak \nupper level ridge dominates.\n\nNext system moves into the Plains for Monday into Wednesday, with\na potent upper level low spinning up and dropping southeast from\nthe Plains into the Lower Mississippi Valley. This places West\nCentral Texas mainly on the drier west side of the system, but\nthere remains some significant uncertainty on this track. Some\nmodels do have the system farther west and bring better rain\nchances into more of the area, especially the eastern third.\n\nPassage of this system will finally bring a stronger cold front\nand a drier air mass. Not going to argue with the lows in the 40s\nfor mid week that the models are showing.",
